  "publication_target": null,
  "pitch": null,
  "ml_idea": "Considered and rejected: a link-prediction model (ESM-2 protein embeddings plus promoter sequence, frozen backbone with a pairwise head) predicting the existence and sign of transcription factor to transcription factor regulatory edges in the ChEA-KG network. The salvageable alternative is not a model but an evaluation: treat ChEA-KG as a prior and test it against independently measured transcription-factor knockdown transcriptomes, asking whether its edges beat TRRUST and motif-based networks at predicting real perturbation outcomes.",
  "effort": {"hours_to_feature_table": 3, "working_set_gb": 0.02, "needs_gpu": false, "peak_ram_gb": 2, "embedding_hours": 1, "cv_run_minutes": 15, "compute_note": "Estimated, not timed, from the verified file sizes (under 20 MB of CSV) and 1,559 protein sequences to embed with a small ESM-2 checkpoint on CPU.", "cheapest_killing_check": "Ask where a single edge's truth value comes from. I traced it: ChEA3 enrichment ranks over RummaGEO gene sets, with no experimental measurement anywhere in the chain. That took ten minutes and kills the project."},
  "verdict": "reject",
  "verdict_reason": "Fails A8. The data is exemplary in every mechanical way - public S3 download with no login, 131,181 rows matching the paper exactly, clean NCBI Gene IDs, no duplicates, no sign conflicts, no missing values, 20 MB total - but every label is manufactured by software. An edge exists because ChEA3 ranked a transcription factor in its top 10 for at least 10 RummaGEO gene sets and that count survived a shuffled-network test; nothing in the file traces back to a physical observation that one factor regulates another. Training a sequence model on it would distil ChEA3's biases with ChEA3's unknown accuracy as the hard ceiling, and the authors themselves say in vitro and in vivo testing would be needed to confirm the links. A3 is also weak (only gene identifiers, no sequences), though that alone would just be a lookup. The one defensible use is as a prior or feature set inside a project whose labels come from measured transcription factor perturbation experiments elsewhere - that is a benchmarking note about this resource, not an ML project built on it."
}
